cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "Q-CIS: a classical coordinate-and-phase classifier (public research release)"
abstract: >-
  Q-CIS is a classical, quantum-inspired learning architecture that represents
  information as coordinates in a state space, assigns each internal state a
  complex-valued amplitude and phase, and decides by the squared modulus of the
  summed amplitudes within each class. The class score is a normalised
  squared-modulus RBF-style expansion with an exact real-valued sine/cosine
  equivalent; complex arithmetic is not required to compute it. No quantum
  computer, physical quantum state, entanglement, or quantum advantage is
  involved or claimed.

  This release contains research documentation, a reference implementation of
  the published equations, deterministic synthetic dataset generators, tests,
  and a reproduction workflow. It does NOT contain the original experiment code,
  raw fit-level data, or the configurations behind the Phase 1-7 figures reported
  in the documentation, so those figures remain author-reported and are not
  independently reproduced here. The reference implementation reproduces the
  published mathematics, not the historical results.
type: software
